   <rms:rms_experience_2_description>Led the architecture and migration of 95% on-premise data to Azure Cloud using Azure Data Factory (ADF) and Azure Databricks (ADB), enabling scalable and cost-efficient data pipelines.
Designed and executed a comprehensive data validation and testing strategy for all in-scope reports, ensuring high data quality and accuracy post-migration.
Built a robust automation framework for data quality checks including null validations, record counts, schema validation, and aggregation checksâ€”reducing manual QA effort by 45%.
Mentored junior QA engineers, supporting their growth through task allocation, technical guidance, and roadblock resolution.
Engineered scalable storage solutions leveraging Azure Data Lake to centralize 2TB of daily ingested data across 10+ pipelines, improving data accessibility and analytical processing speed by 60% over 18 months.
Integrated Azure Synapse Analytics with existing Azure Data Lake architecture to unify batch and real-time analytics on 2TB daily data, reducing dashboard latency by 35% and supporting 
Managed migration of 1PB historical data to Azure Blob Storage over 12 months using AzCopy and Python scripts, optimizing storage costs by 40% and supporting seamless integration with ADF-based ETL workflows.</rms:rms_experience_2_description>
